    "q-183279": {
      "dom_id": "step-q183279",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$\\,$ $x$ is not a prime number, or $x$ is odd.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is a prime number\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is an odd integer",
      "worked_solution": "The sentence \n\n$\\,$ $x$ is not a prime number.\n\n can be expressed symbolically as $¬P.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is expressed symbolically as \n\n$$\n¬P∨Q.\n$$",
