    "q-183273": {
      "dom_id": "step-q183273",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$\\,$ $x$ is neither divisible by $2$ nor divisible by $3.$\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is divisible by $2$\n\n- $Q(x):$  $x$ is divisible by $3$",
      "worked_solution": "The given sentence is equivalent to the following sentence: \n\n$\\,$ $x$ is not divisible by $2$, and $x$ is not divisible by $3.$\n\nLet's break our sentence down into individual statements:\n\n- The statement \"$x$ is not divisible by $2$\" can be expressed symbolically as $¬P.$\n\n- The statement \"$x$ is not divisible by $3$\" can be expressed symbolically as $¬Q.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is expressed symbolically as\n\n$$\n¬P∧¬Q.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
