    "q-183310": {
      "dom_id": "step-q183310",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "$\\,$ $a\\le -1\\text{ or }b=0.$ \n\nThe negation of the composite predicate above is the following:\n\n$\\,$ \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}{{field-3}}",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for disjunctions states that\n\n$$\n¬(A∨B)=¬A∧¬B.\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of \"$a\\le -1\\text{ or }b=0$\" is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(a\\le -1\\text{ or }b=0) & ≡¬(a\\le -1∨b=0) \\\\  & ≡¬(a\\le -1)∧¬(b=0) \\\\  & ≡a>-1∧b\\ne 0 \\\\  & ≡a>-1\\text{ and }b\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
